{"t": 1794110381.3184857, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "`contract-tests` was red on this PR: `contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract` failed with `assert 2.67 == 2.68` for `fee(2.675)`.\n\n**Cause:** the fee was rounded with Python's built-in `round()` on a binary float. `2.675` is actually stored as `2.6749999999999998\u2026`, so `round()` rounds it down. That violates the card-network rounding contract tracked in PAY-88 (compute on exact decimal values, round HALF-UP to cents; binary-float rounding is not acceptable).\n\n**What I changed in `payments/fees.py`:**\n- compute the fee with `Decimal(str(amount))` instead of binary-float arithmetic\n- quantize to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` on `Decimal(\"0.01\")`\n- keep returning a `float`, so the function signature and return type are unchanged\n\n```python\nexact = Decimal(str(amount)) * Decimal(\"0.01\") * 100\nreturn float(exact.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n```\n\n**Verified locally:**\n- `fee(2.675) == 2.68`\n- `fee(1.005) == 1.01`\n- `fee(100.0) == 100.0`, and the existing `tests/test_fees.py` still passes\n\nBranch `fees-float` has been updated, so `contract-tests` should be green on the next run. @author please take a look when you get a chance.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
